Yes. If you have a disability that makes it hard to read, see, hear, or understand material, the university can change it into a format that works for you.
For example, they can:
Turn text into audio
Add captions to videos
Make text larger or screen-reader friendly
They can share this with you online (e.g., via email), and you can use it for study or personal use.
The only limits are:
The material should only be shared with students who need it
The university may check if an accessible version already exists before making one

